{"type": "item", "run_id": "20260930T014612Z-routine", "option": "routine", "item_id": "5cc8f180d7d24936a05928ca", "title": "How Diffusion Controller unifies and simplifies AI image generation", "url": "https://research.google/blog/how-diffusion-controller-unifies-and-simplifies-ai-image-generation/", "source": "The latest research from Google", "published": "2026-09-29T18:38:27+00:00", "is_ai": 0.99, "worthiness": 0.8025, "worthiness_confidence": 0.34, "final_score": 0.8025, "bucket": "high", "full_text": true, "content_source": "article_fetch", "text_chars": 7681, "delivered": true, "summary": "Google Research introduced Diffusion Controller, a lightweight adapter network that steers image generation toward better prompt alignment without modifying base models. It works as a \"steering damper\" that can attach to closed-source models, unifying previously disconnected inference-time and fine-tuning techniques into a single control framework. The approach achieved 90% win rates over baselines in white-box settings and outperformed LoRA in gray-box scenarios using Human Preference Score metrics. Key takeaway: engineers can now control even restricted models by injecting microscopic trajectory corrections during denoising, enabling precise prompt adherence while preserving image quality through a single, mathematically principled system.", "jev_ms": 566.4, "jev_input_tokens": 2099, "jev_cost": 8.8158e-05, "llm_ms": 2839.9, "llm_cost": 0.002482, "errors": []}
{"type": "item", "run_id": "20260930T014612Z-routine", "option": "routine", "item_id": "0e6ecf3b3252b9526d4c38c7", "title": "Introducing Quine: An AI research system designed for the complexity of biology", "url": "https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/research/blog/introducing-quine-an-ai-research-system-designed-for-the-complexity-of-biology/", "source": "Microsoft Research", "published": "2026-09-29T14:00:02+00:00", "is_ai": 0.97, "worthiness": 0.7725, "worthiness_confidence": 0.71, "final_score": 0.7725, "bucket": "high", "full_text": true, "content_source": "feed_full_text", "text_chars": 12213, "delivered": true, "summary": "Microsoft introduced Quine, a multimodal AI system combining a world model of biology with tools connecting models, literature, and wet-lab experiments. Working with Broad Institute researchers on pancreatic cancer, Quine predicted compounds to shift tumor cell states, validating top candidates in one weekend versus months of traditional work. The system learns jointly across genomics, proteins, chemistry, cell state, and imaging modalities, enabling cross-domain reasoning. Key takeaway: multimodal training strengthens generalization by capturing relationships across biological scales rather than siloing specialist models. The Quine Fellows program now offers scientists early access.", "jev_ms": 213.7, "jev_input_tokens": 2879, "jev_cost": 0.000120918, "llm_ms": 3049.7, "llm_cost": 0.003217, "errors": []}
